/T (By contrast, the rate of young people who are neither in education nor employment \(NEET\) among Bangladeshis aged 18 to 24 is declining, although it is still high: 33.4%, down 3.4% compared to the previous year. This is higher than the figure recorded for non-EU citizens \(24.9%\) and young Italians \(14.3%\), which is particularly significant among the female members of the community: 69.7%, indicating difficulties in the social and professional integration of young women.)
