/T (In 2024, 9,726 Bangladeshi citizens acquired citizenship \(4.9% of total third-country nationals\), showing a sharp increase compared to the previous year \(+20.6%\). In most cases, citizenship was acquired through transmission from parents, turning of age of 18, or ius sanguinis, which account for about half of the cases \(50.6%\). Naturalization accounts for 44.1% of acquisitions, while only 5.3% are linked to marriage to an Italian citizen.)
/E (In 2024, 9,726 Bangladeshi citizens acquired citizenship \(4.9% of total third-country nationals\), showing a sharp increase compared to the previous year \(+20.6%\). In most cases, citizenship was acquired through transmission from parents, turning of age of 18, or ius sanguinis, which account for about half of the cases \(50.6%\). Naturalization accounts for 44.1% of acquisitions, while only 5.3% are linked to marriage to an Italian citizen.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
