/T (Financial inclusion, defined as access to and proper use of a variety of financial instruments, is an enabling factor for the initiation and consolidation of the socio-economic integration process of individuals and their families. At the heart of this development process is access to a current account and a payment system, in addition to increasingly complex needs corresponding to an equal number of financial instruments, including access to credit, investments, forms of accumulation, and savings protection.)
/E (Financial inclusion, defined as access to and proper use of a variety of financial instruments, is an enabling factor for the initiation and consolidation of the socio-economic integration process of individuals and their families. At the heart of this development process is access to a current account and a payment system, in addition to increasingly complex needs corresponding to an equal number of financial instruments, including access to credit, investments, forms of accumulation, and savings protection.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
