/Title (The territorial distribution of Bangladeshi citizens differs significantly from that of the whole of the non-EU population in Italy, with a lower concentration in Northern Italy \(46.1% compared to 59.8%\), and a higher presence in Central Italy \(31.7% compared to 23.1%\) and in Southern Italy and the Islands \(22.2% against 17.1%\). In particular, Lazio is home to 22% of the community, with a high concentration in the metropolitan city of Rome, which hosts 37,905 Bangladeshis, 19.4% of the total. It is followed by Lombardy \(15.1%\) and Veneto \(10.8%\), while in the south, Campania \(8.5%\) and Sicily \(6.8%\) are the regions with the highest number of Bangladeshis.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2356 0 R
/Prev 2371 0 R
>>
endobj
