/Title (There remains a significant gender imbalance within the community: 76.7% are men and 23.3% are women, placing it second among the principal communities with the lowest female presence, outnumbered only by the Pakistani community. This figure can be traced back to the characteristics of Bangladeshi migration: it is generally young men who migrate, supporting their families in their country of origin through remittances, and returning home periodically. Only when an adequate level of economic and social stability has been achieved does family reunification take place.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2358 0 R
/Next 2388 0 R
>>
